body:
The mapping from existing view data to ViewDesigner columns uses array index as the `order` property (line 88), but if the existing view columns are sparse or out of order, this could create unintended column ordering.

Additionally, the code maps `existingView.columns` which is an array of strings to ViewDesignerColumn objects, but doesn't preserve any existing width, visibility, or other column configuration that might have been stored. If views can have richer column definitions in the future, this mapping will lose that data.

Consider checking if the existing column data is already in the ViewDesignerColumn format before mapping, or preserve any additional properties that may exist.
```suggestion
            ? existingView.columns.map((c: any, i: number) => {
                // If the column is already an object, preserve its properties
                if (c && typeof c === 'object') {
                  const col: any = { ...c };

                  // Ensure order is set, but do not override an explicit numeric order
                  if (typeof col.order !== 'number') {
                    col.order = col.order ?? i;
                  }

                  // Ensure label is set, preferring existing label
                  if (col.label == null) {
                    const fieldName = col.field ?? col.name;
                    col.label =
                      availableFields.find((f: any) => f.name === fieldName)?.label ??
                      fieldName;
                  }

                  // Default visible to true if not explicitly boolean
                  if (typeof col.visible !== 'boolean') {
                    col.visible = col.visible ?? true;
                  }

                  return col;
                }

                // Legacy case: column is a string (field name) or other primitive
                const fieldName = String(c);
                return {
                  field: fieldName,
                  label:
                    availableFields.find((f: any) => f.name === fieldName)?.label ??
                    fieldName,
                  visible: true,
                  order: i,
                };
              })
```
